    backgroundMusic: "gentle",
    ttsScript: "Find a comfortable position... where you can be still... and attentive... ...Gently close your eyes... and take a slow, deep breath in... and a long, gentle exhale out... ...Allow your body to relax... and your mind to quiet... ...Today, we turn to a profound truth... from Viktor Frankl's reflections on suffering and meaning... ...'Forces beyond your control can take away everything you possess except one thing, your freedom to choose how you will respond to the situation.'... ...This meditation invites you to connect with that indestructible freedom... within yourself... ...Bring to mind a challenge... a difficulty... or a painful experience you have faced... or are currently facing... ...Notice the emotions that arise... the discomfort... the frustration... the sadness... ...Acknowledge these feelings fully... without trying to push them away... ...Now... recognize that even in the midst of this struggle... you have a choice... ...You have the freedom to choose your attitude... your perspective... your ultimate response... ...This freedom is your final human liberty... it cannot be taken from you... ...Consider how your response... to this suffering... can give it meaning... ...Suffering in itself... is meaningless... but we give our suffering meaning... by the way in which we respond to it... ...Will you respond with bitterness?... or with courage?... ...With despair?... or with dignity?... ...Picture yourself... standing firm... in your inner resolve... ...Even if the external circumstances are harsh... imagine your inner world remaining strong... resilient... ...This is not about denying pain... but about finding a higher purpose... a greater understanding... within the pain... ...Remind yourself: 'I cannot control what happens to me... but I can always control what I will feel and do about what happens to me.'... ...Feel the empowering truth of this statement... resonating through your entire being... ...It is in this choice... that your human dignity is preserved... and your inner strength revealed... ...Take another deep, grounding breath... committing to finding meaning and choosing your response... no matter the circumstance... ...When you are ready... gently open your eyes... carrying this profound sense of inner freedom and dignity into your day...",
