    phase: "all",
    backgroundMusic: "gentle",
    ttsScript: "Settle into a comfortable posture... allowing your body to soften and relax... ...Gently close your eyes... and take a deep, slow breath... ...Exhale completely... letting go of any tension... ...Again... deeply inhale... and slowly exhale... ...Feeling yourself arrive fully... in this precious moment... ...Today, we'll explore 'the power of now'... the profound truth that the present moment... is all there ever is... ...Our minds often dwell in the past... rehashing memories... or project into the future... planning... worrying... anticipating... ...But real life... your life... is only happening... right now... ...Bring your attention to the simplest sensations of this moment... ...The subtle sounds around you... ...The feeling of the air on your skin... ...The gentle rise and fall of your breath... ...Don't label them... don't judge them... just allow them to simply 'be'... and you, to simply 'be' with them... ...As thoughts arise... like clouds passing in the sky... simply observe them... without engagement... ...Notice the space... between your thoughts... the quiet... the stillness... ...This stillness... this pure awareness... is your essence... your true self... ...It is timeless... unchanging... always present... ...Feel yourself dissolving... into this pure presence... ...Let go of your story... your identity... your worries... even for a few moments... ...There's nowhere to go... nothing to do... nothing to become... ...You are simply... here... ...In this 'now'... there is a deep peace... a profound sense of inner joy... ...This is not a happiness that depends on external circumstances... but a timeless joy... inherent to your being... ...Stay with this feeling... this timeless presence... for a few more breaths... ...Allow it to permeate every cell of your body... ...'You are here to enable the divine purpose of the universe to unfold. That is how important you are!'... ...This unfolding happens... in the Now... ...Take one final, deep breath... affirming your connection to this eternal present... ...As you exhale, softly open your eyes... carrying this profound 'now-awareness' with you into the rest of your day...",
