    phase: "all",
    backgroundMusic: "none",
    ttsScript: "Find a place where you can be undisturbed for a few minutes... ideally outdoors... or near a window... ...Settle into a comfortable posture... allowing your eyes to gently close... or to softly gaze at a neutral point... ...Take a slow, deep breath in through your nose... and a long, gentle exhale out through your mouth... ...Repeat this... feeling your body soften... and your mind begin to quiet... ...In our modern world... we are constantly seeking stimulation... constantly avoiding 'boredom'... ...But today, we invite boredom... as a path to mental clarity and deeper presence... ...Release the urge to reach for a device... to plan... to analyze... ...Simply 'be' in this present moment... ...Allow your mind to truly have nothing specific to do... no task to complete... no problem to solve... ...Notice what happens... ...Perhaps your mind will still chatter... trying to fill the void... trying to find something to 'do'... ...Gently observe these impulses... without judgment... then let them go... ...Bring your attention to your surroundings... especially if you are outdoors... ...Listen to the subtle sounds around you... ...The distant hum of traffic... the rustle of leaves... the chirping of birds... ...Feel the temperature of the air on your skin... ...Observe the textures... the colors... the patterns in nature... ...Do not label them... do not evaluate them... simply observe... with a quiet, open curiosity... ...This is not a void... but a space of potential... a space where your mind can reset... can wander freely... and then return to clarity... ...Embrace the quiet... the stillness... the simplicity of just being... in an unstimulating environment... ...Allow your attention to soften and expand... taking it all in... ...Feel the richness... in the seemingly 'nothing' of this moment... ...This 'boredom' is a doorway... to deeper awareness... to creativity... to a more authentic connection with yourself and the world... ...Take one more slow, deep breath... feeling a renewed sense of openness and mental space... ...As you exhale... gently open your eyes... carrying this curiosity and clarity into your day... ...And remember... this deliberate pause... this embracing of simple observation... is always available to you...",
