    ttsScript: "Find a comfortable position... allowing your body to soften... and your breath to settle... ...Gently close your eyes... and take a deep, slow breath in... and a long, gentle exhale out... ...Allow yourself to be fully present... in this moment... ...Today, we'll practice a timeless reflection... a 'meditation on mortality.'... ...This is not to invite fear... but to cultivate a profound appreciation for life... and to clarify what truly matters... ...The Stoics understood that by contemplating our finite nature... we are spurred to live more purposefully... and virtuously... ...Bring to awareness... the simple fact... that life is impermanent... ...Every moment is precious... every day a gift... ...Imagine yourself... looking back on your life... from a distant future point... ...What would you wish you had done more of?... ...Less of?... ...Who would you wish you had connected with more deeply?... ...What values would you wish you had lived by... more consistently?... ...This perspective... offers immense clarity... ...It helps us to shed the trivial... the distracting... and to focus on the essential... ...Feel a gentle urgenc... not anxiety... but a warm invitation... to live fully... right now... ...To express love... to pursue knowledge... to embody kindness... to face challenges with courage... ...You have the freedom to choose... how you will spend this precious, finite time... ...What legacy do you wish to create... not necessarily for the world... but for your own inner peace and integrity?... ...Let go of regrets about the past... and anxieties about the distant future... ...Your power... resides in this present moment... ...The quality of your current actions... your present choices... defines the richness of your life... ...Take a deep, grounding breath... internalizing a sense of purpose and appreciation... ...As you exhale, affirm to yourself: 'I embrace impermanence to live purposefully and virtuously now.'.... ...When you are ready... gently open your eyes... carrying this profound awareness into the rest of your day...",
